              77.0,
              1283.0
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "The prior codification is necessary because FANNs only handle values within the closed interval  $ [0, 1] $. Therefore, the actual input and output values that the net receives and obtains are 0's and 1's. This codification–decodification is done by the encoder class attached to the machine agent (see Fig. 5). Therefore, the FANN has six processing units in the input layer, which are in charge of dealing exclusively with the raw material family. The totality of discrete values contained in the input and output sets were",
